92186265919 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265920 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329646 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329647 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345121 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345122 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345123 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115064 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115234 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116103 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116104 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116105 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116106 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116107 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186116125 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1045 "Properties of Matrix Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186116103 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050128 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186115476 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f5bf1856-47b4-5455-be99-90d735981501" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116103 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116104 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116103 #edb/ref 1061 16195 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116103 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b9aabff-e92b-5507-9327-e103c1c53a12" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116103 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116492 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116104 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116105 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116104 #edb/ref 1061 16196 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116104 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f6895fd-de2c-5b1d-96fd-486f6bcbc9a7" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116104 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115232 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116105 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116106 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116105 #edb/ref 1061 16197 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116105 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e49acfe6-644b-55a4-86c6-154201b20646" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116105 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116106 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116125 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116106 #edb/ref 1061 16198 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116106 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "31661944-ebfa-574b-9783-47e41b70b808" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116106 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115233 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116107 #edb/ref 1061 16199 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116107 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "375c5e0d-680a-5465-afbc-b89498f3e772" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116107 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115234 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116125 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116107 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116125 #edb/ref 1061 17045 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116125 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c85ef919-914b-57cc-ab1b-19cb7cd36e6e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116125 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116498 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116492 #edb/ref 1064 "We have already seen some properties of matrix multiplication. For example, multiplying any $n \\times n$ square matrix $A$ by the identity matrix $I_n$ will leave it unchanged:\n\n$$\nA I_n = I_n A = A.\n$$\n\nAlso, matrix multiplication follows the **distributive laws**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)C & =AC+BC, \\\\ C(A+B) & =CA+CB.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116492 #edb/ref 1065 2997 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116492 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "60b5c83f-3d84-5140-80c7-c4640bea28b0" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116492 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116493 #edb/ref 1064 "If $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are three matrices that are conformable for multiplication, then they follow the **associative law**:\n\n$$\n\\left( AB\\right) C = A\\left( BC\\right)\n$$\n\nSo, when we wish to compute a product $ABC,$ we don't always have to start by multiplying $AB.$ Alternatively, we can start by multiplying $BC,$ and then multiply $A$ by the result. \n\nSometimes rearranging the parentheses might make the computations slightly easier." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116493 #edb/ref 1065 2998 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116493 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "31c195bb-9066-55bf-ae02-9de81da2b7bb" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116493 #edb/ref 1067 "The Associative Law for Matrix Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116498 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, matrix multiplication is **not** commutative. In other words, given two general matrices $A$ and $B$ that are conformable for multiplication, we have\n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nHowever, some particular matrices may satisfy this property. For instance, $AI = IA$ (where $I$ is the identity matrix)." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116498 #edb/ref 1065 3129 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116498 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4e92439e-2fc7-59ca-beb8-2ace6a7d3e71" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186116498 #edb/ref 1067 "Matrix Multiplication Is Not Commutative in General" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152185 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050831 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152777 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152781 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292885 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295183 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [175921861521