17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186291893 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186291893 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186291113 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186291893 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "2daa9284-83e4-5449-8185-db49a6c674e4" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291242 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292208 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292208 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292208 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186291242 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292208 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "956ba8d7-fa47-5f7a-b145-9f5e1da669dd" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291893 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292208 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1069 "q-275128" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/99/992be4e67316804381ffc38860d2eaf23fd4a93cfe22ec4918c30c41e34ade57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n\n$-\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nand \n$\\mu =$\n\n$-\\frac{5}{2}$\n\n." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d447ec6b-433a-5b79-9c9d-143f856c643d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186292813 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/c0/c0f7f4df52373ca602aff41c97a5b8413f510353874540b76147c527a2f4b18c.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=\\frac{1}{2}|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-\\frac{1}{2}r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=\\frac{5}{2}|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-\\frac{5}{2}s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-\\frac{1}{